'''Azazel''' is a [[character]] unlocked by making three {{R|Devil Room}} deals in one run. He starts with 3 {{E|Black Heart}}s, {{p|0 - The Fool}}, [[flight]], and a short-ranged version of {{i|Brimstone}} that deals damage {{dlcalt|13|r=9}} times in one second.

Despite starting with no [[Red Heart container]]s, Azazel is capable of gaining them.

== Notes ==
* Azazel suffers from a very short range, in return for better mobility through flight and high speed, high-power bursts of damage with his Brimstone-like attack, and a room clear upon the loss of a {{E|Black Heart}}.
* Azazel's flight is a very powerful asset, allowing him to accomplish many tasks and save resources:
** Due to his flight, Azazel takes damage only when leaving a {{R|Curse Room}}. He can also use his starting card, {{p|0 - The Fool}}, to avoid the cost for one room entirely.
** Flight allows him to reach [[pickups]] across obstacles and gaps.
** Flight helps in avoiding enemies in general.
* Azazel's mini-Brimstone's charge is kept across rooms, saving precious charging time.
* {{dlc+|r}} If Azazel dies in [[Repentance Co-Op|co-op]], his ghost will also fire a short Brimstone.{{dlc-}}

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}}: Azazel's Brimstone beam doubles in width, equal to the width of {{i|Mega Blast}}. No effect on damage.
* {{i|Dead Eye|r}}: Damage can be gained if Azazel fires tears via items like {{i|Lead Pencil}} or {{i|Isaac's Tears}}.
* {{i|Ipecac|r}}: The tear delay remains unchanged, and the end of the beam is explosive. No tear is fired.
* {{i|Jacob's Ladder|r}}: The Brimstone is electrified and sparks can connect with enemies.
* {{i|Lead Pencil|r}}: Azazel will fire a low-range Monstro's Lung-like barrage of 12 tears occasionally.
* {{dlc|a}}{{i|Mysterious Liquid}}: Creep will spawn at the edge of the laser.
* {{i|Technology Zero}}: Has no effect.

* The following items override Azazel's short-ranged Brimstone:
** {{i|Dr. Fetus}}
** {{i|Epic Fetus}}
** {{i|Haemolacria}}
** {{i|Mom's Knife}}
** {{i|Spirit Sword}}

=== Good Items ===
* {{i|20/20|a}}: Doubles lasers without increasing tear delay.
* {{i|Abaddon}}: Aside from the lack of Angel Rooms, it provides no downside. As it costs 3 Soul Hearts, it will add 3 Black Hearts to his health bar, increase damage and speed, and give his Brimstone laser a fear effect.
** {{dlc|r}} This is no longer the case, as the amount of Black Hearts given by Abaddon is now based on the amount of Red Hearts it removes.
* {{i|Brimstone}}: Gives Azazel the long-range version. It also increases fire rate since Brimstone's fire rate multiplier is ×1/3 and Azazel's is ×0.267.
* {{i|Chocolate Milk}}: {{dlcalt|Reduces charge time|r=His Brimstone laser takes longer to be fully charged but can be released anytime. Width and damage of the laser increases at higher charges. Width scales from 50% at minimum charge to 160% at maximum charge. damage scales from 25% at minimum charge to 250% at maximum charge. Unlike with normal tears, the tears stat does not directly affect maximum or minimum damage}}.
* {{i|Circle of Protection}}: The circle is nearly the same size as Azazel's laser, adding extra damage.
* {{I|Continuum|r}}: The range of Azazel's short Brimstone is increased and wraps around the screen, though without other significant range boosts, it doesn't wrap far enough to reach into the room.
* {{I|Cricket's Body|r}}: Adds a scatter of blood tears from Azazel's Brimstone's landing point.
* {{i|Eye of the Occult}}: Azazel's Brimstone becomes a lasso, auto-fired at a controllable target. Press Fire to start and Drop to stop.
* {{i|Marked|dlc=r}}: Azazel's Brimstone is auto-fired in the direction of a controllable target. Press Fire to start and Drop to stop.
* {{i|Hemoptysis}}: Enemies hit by the sneeze will gain a curse that increases the damage Azazel's beam deals to 2× and +3 flat damage. Enemies who die to his beam under the curse will explode, dealing damage and spreading the curse to nearby enemies.
* {{i|The Inner Eye}} / {{i|Mutant Spider}}: Shoots multiple mini-Brimstone lasers with a massively increased tear delay.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: Gives a Brimstone ring (whether Azazel has the short or long-ranged version of it) giving him the ability to damage many enemies at a time due to its size, and negates Azazel's short range, however, it halves Azazel's damage.
* {{i|Mom's Eye}}: Allows Azazel to shoot two beams, one of which is shot behind him.
* {{i|Monstro's Lung|a}}: Gives several additional Brimstone beams around Azazel.
* {{i|My Reflection}}: Greatly increases the range of Azazel's mini-Brimstone.
** {{dlc|anr}} Greatly increases the Brimstone laser's range and makes the laser curve as Azazel moves around the room.
** {{dlc|r}} Greatly increases the Brimstone laser's range and makes the laser double back on itself to land behind Azazel.
* {{i|Number One}}: Slightly decreases Azazel's range but significantly decreases the charge time of Azazel's Brimstone. It also turns Azazel's laser yellow.
* {{i|The Parasite|r}}: Creates 2 short lasers upon hitting the first enemy, or a wall. The derivative lasers follow the same movement of regular parasite shots.
* {{i|Proptosis}}: Doubles the Brimstone laser's damage without any downsides.
** {{dlc|a}} The beam will decrease in damage the further it travels, but Proptosis still greatly increases damage at close range.
*** {{dlc|r}} Due to an oversight, Proptosis deals way more damage than it should with lasers. At long range, it deals ×6 damage, and at close range, it can deal up to ×7.5. Base Azazel + Proptosis can deal over 350 damage in one beam, which can kill {{e|Chub}} in one laser.
* {{i|Rubber Cement|a}}: Allows Azazel's laser to bounce off of walls. Unlike Azazel's normal mini-Brimstone, beams that bounce off walls have infinite range but deal only half of their damage.
** {{dlc|r}} The beam will no longer turn into regular {{i|Brimstone}} upon bouncing off a wall. It will instead turn into his mini-Brimstone.
* {{i|Sad Bombs}}: Shoots 10 short-ranged Brimstone beams around the explosion point, which deals enormous amounts of damage.
* {{i|Tammy's Head}}: Shoots 10 short-ranged Brimstone beams around him, which deal enormous amounts of damage.
* {{t|Tape Worm}}: Greatly increases the Brimstone laser's range.
* {{i|Technology|a}}: Works like it does with normal Brimstone, changing the visual effect and granting the +50% damage multiplier.
* {{i|Technology 2}}: Provides a laser while Brimstone is charging, allowing the player to do damage while the charge occurs. However, {{dlcalt|this also decreases the damage and tear rate of Azazel's Brimstone|r=this also decreases the tear rate of Azazel's Brimstone}}.
* {{i|Tech X|r}}: Makes Azazel fire a ring-shaped Brimstone beam but decrease his damage a bit.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: Changes the path of Azazel's Brimstone into a circle, giving it an area of effect. The range increase becomes especially powerful if you add a homing tears effect.
* {{i|Varicose Veins|dlc=a+}}: Causes a short Brimstone explosion around the player upon getting damaged.
* {{i|C Section}}: Fires 4 fetuses on top of his Brimstone.

=== Bad Items ===
* {{i|The Wiz}}: While useful in some situations, enemies such as The Thing or other Creeps will be dangerous.
* Items that respawn Azazel as a different character, including {{i|Ankh}}, {{i|Lazarus' Rags}}, and {{i|Judas' Shadow}} will remove the ability to fly and the Brimstone laser.
* Items that break Rocks, like {{i|Leo}} or {{i|Thunder Thighs}}, nullify part of the advantage Azazel gains from flight, as he will no longer be able to hover over rocks to avoid enemy projectiles.
* Items that give flight will have no real effect, since Azazel has a built-in ability to fly.
* {{i|Kidney Stone|dlc=nr}}: Only reduces Azazel's speed and shortens Brimstone's range.

* The following items have their effect nullified with Azazel's short-ranged Brimstone:
** {{i|Cursed Eye}}
** {{i|Compound Fracture}}
** {{i|Cupid's Arrow}}
** {{i|Ouija Board}}
** {{t|Pulse Worm}}
** {{i|Pupula Duplex}}
** {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Strange Attractor}} (Until {{i|Anti-Gravity}} is picked up)
** {{i|Trisagion}}
** {{i|Tropicamide}}
** {{i|Neptunus}}

